Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml

# Secrets stay out of image layers; runtime env comes from compose env_file,
# build-time public values come from compose build args
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Real financial data + local databases must NEVER enter image layers (they'd ship in the deploy tar).
# The data dir is a runtime bind-mount; DBs are durable-on-host (SQLite) or rebuildable (DuckDB).
/data
**/*.duckdb
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
